{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b770-2bd1-7eca-805e-b60840b1e8cf","session_id":"01a1b76f-c764-7902-805e-3362c00095cd","message":{"id":"01a1b7702bd07b4098a3d3fa627f0ac7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Important observations:\n\n1. `ci-results.json` has 15 results (A-1 through A-15), all passed=true, exitCode=0, lastLine \"AC-015 OK\" etc. and output is just the OK line. Note: the output is just \"AC-015 OK\" (single line). \n\nWait — but the acceptance.md has 20 commands: A-1..A-15 (15 commands), plus R-1, R-2, R-3, R-4, R-5 (5 gate commands) = 20 total. But ci-results.json only has 15 entries (A-1..A-15). The R-1..R-5 gates are NOT in ci-results.json!\n\nHmm. Let me re-read. The impl.md says \"逐条执行了 acceptance.md 里的全部 20 段命令\" and lists R-1..R-5 results. But ci-results.json only has 15 entries. So the execution evidence for R-1..R-5 gates is missing from ci-results.json.\n\nWait, let me carefully count. ci-results.json \"results\" array: A-1, A-2, A-3, A-4, A-5, A-6, A-7, A-8, A-9, A-10, A-11, A-12, A-13, A-14, A-15 = 15 entries. \"passed\": 15, \"total\": 15.\n\nSo the CI runner only ran the 15 AC commands (A-1..A-15), not the 5 repository gates R-1..R-5.\n\nThis is significant. The acceptance.md has 20 commands total (15 AC + 5 gates). The verdict needs to judge each acceptance item. The user says: \"逐条核对 acceptance.md，独立判断是否真的满足\" (check each acceptance.md item one by one, independently judge whether truly satisfied). And the CI execution evidence standard: \"编排方已用 PowerShell 7 执行过验收命令，结果在 <task>/ci-results.json（每条命令、退出码、输出）。这些就是「执行类」验收项的有效运行证据，直接引用即可，不必自己重跑。\" — \"The orchestrator ran the acceptance commands with PowerShell 7, results in ci-results.json. These are valid running evidence for 'execution-type' acceptance items. Only when CI results are missing, or clearly contradict the code, mark that item as unable to confirm and write finding; otherwise use read-only methods to independently verify implementation and spec consistency.\"\n\nSo for \"execution-type\" acceptance items, I should cite ci-results.json. But the CI results only cover 15 of 20 commands. The R-1..R-5 gates need to be verified via read-only methods (read files, compute hashes, verify line numbers). \n\nActually, the instruction says \"其余请用只读方式（读文件、算哈希、核对行号）独立验证实现与规格是否一致\" (for the rest, use read-only methods to independently verify implementation and spec consistency). So \"the rest\" — items that are not execution-type — should be verified read-only. But also the R-1..R-5 gates are execution-type commands but they're missing from CI. Hmm.\n\nLet me reconsider. The phrase \"只有 CI 结果缺失、或与代码明显矛盾时，才把该项标为无法确认并写 finding\" (Only when CI results are missing, or clearly contradict the code, mark that item as unable to confirm and write a finding). This suggests that if CI results for an item are missing, I should mark it as \"unable to confirm\" and write a finding.\n\nBut wait — that seems to apply specifically to \"执行类\" (execution-type) items. For R-1..R-5 gates, are those \"execution-type\"? Yes, they are commands. But the CI didn't run them. However, the gates can be verified read-only too in many cases (R-3 is a pure file-content check, R-4 is a pure file-content check — these can be fully verified by reading files). R-1, R-2, R-5 involve running scripts.\n\nLet me think about the intent here. The user is telling me: don't judge needs_revision just because MY environment lacks pwsh7 or temp file perms. The CI results are the authoritative execution evidence. For items where CI results exist, cite them. For items where CI results are missing or contradict code, mark as unconfirmable + finding. For the rest (read-only verifiable things), verify by reading.\n\nSo I need to be careful. Let me figure out the exact structure.\n\nActually, let me re-read very carefully:\n\n\"【执行证据口径】编排方已用 PowerShell 7 执行过验收命令，结果在 <task>/ci-results.json（每条命令、退出码、输出）。这些就是「执行类」验收项的有效运行证据，直接引用即可，不必自己重跑。你的评审环境可能缺 pwsh 7、或缺临时文件权限——这不能作为判 needs_revision 的理由。只有 CI 结果缺失、或与代码明显矛盾时，才把该项标为无法确认并写 finding；其余请用只读方式（读文件、算哈希、核对行号）独立验证实现与规格是否一致。\"\n\nTranslation: \"[Execution evidence standard] The orchestrator has run the acceptance commands with PowerShell 7, results in <task>/ci-results.json (each command, exit code, output). These are the valid running evidence for 'execution-type' acceptance items, cite them directly, no need to re-run. Your review environment may lack pwsh 7, or lack temp file permissions — this cannot be a reason to judge needs_revision. Only when CI results are missing, or clearly contradict the code, mark that item as unable to confirm and write a finding; for the rest use read-only methods (read files, compute hashes, verify line numbers) to independently verify implementation and spec consistency.\"\n\nOK so the key insight: there's a concern that a reviewer might judge needs_revision just because they can't run commands. The user says: that's not a valid reason. The CI results ARE the execution evidence. \n\nSo I should:\n- For each acceptance item, if it's an execution-type item with a CI result → cite it (passed).\n- For items without CI results → I need to verify read-only. If read-only verification confirms spec consistency, that's fine. But the phrase \"只有 CI 结果缺失...才把该项标为无法确认并写 finding\" suggests that if CI results are missing, I should mark it \"unable to confirm\" and write a finding.\n\nHmm, but that seems to conflict with \"其余请用只读方式...独立验证\". Let me parse: \"只有 [CI 结果缺失、或与代码明显矛盾] 时，才把该项标为无法确认并写 finding；其余请用只读方式...独立验证实现与规格是否一致。\"\n\nSo: \n- Condition A: CI results missing OR clearly contradict code → mark item \"unable to confirm\" + write finding\n- Otherwise (condition B, \"其余\"): use read-only methods to independently verify implementation/spec consistency.\n\nWait but \"其余\" (the rest) could mean \"the rest of the items\" or \"the rest of the verification work\". I think it means: for all other items (i.e., where CI results exist and don't contradict), use read-only methods to independently verify imp