{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b771-55fe-7d12-9856-7006d3ed72a5","session_id":"01a1b76f-c764-7902-805e-3362c00095cd","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b90ae9f0f26d3f8a","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→import { systemNow } from './context.mjs'\n   2→import { round3, normalizeQuota, evaluatePools } from './pools.mjs'\n   3→\n   4→export { round3 }\n   5→\n   6→export const DEFAULT_PRICES = { input_per_mtok: 0, output_per_mtok: 0 }\n   7→\n   8→export function normalizePrices(m = {}) {\n   9→  const p = m.prices || {}\n  10→  return {\n  11→    input_per_mtok: Number(p.input_per_mtok ?? DEFAULT_PRICES.input_per_mtok),\n  12→    output_per_mtok: Number(p.output_per_mtok ?? DEFAULT_PRICES.output_per_mtok),\n  13→  }\n  14→}\n  15→\n  16→export function estimateCost({ input_tokens = 0, output_tokens = 0, prices = DEFAULT_PRICES }) {\n  17→  const p = { ...DEFAULT_PRICES, ...prices }\n  18→  return (Number(input_tokens) / 1e6) * p.input_per_mtok + (Number(output_tokens) / 1e6) * p.output_per_mtok\n  19→}\n  20→\n  21→/**\n  22→ * Deterministic, intentionally simple forecast. Unknown is a first-class state.\n  23→ * @deprecated Superseded by buildForecast; kept until lib/select.mjs migrates (T-007).\n  24→ */\n  25→export function forecast({ records = [], model, prices, quota = null, now = systemNow() } = {}) {\n  26→  const rows = records.filter((r) => !model || r.model === model)\n  27→  const samples = rows.map((r) => ({\n  28→    at: Date.parse(r.at || 0), input: Number(r.input_tokens || 0), output: Number(r.output_tokens || 0),\n  29→    cost: Number(r.cost_usd ?? estimateCost({ input_tokens: r.input_tokens, output_tokens: r.output_tokens, prices })),\n  30→  })).filter((r) => Number.isFinite(r.at) && r.at > 0)\n  31→  if (!samples.length) {\n  32→    return { status: 'unknown', samples: 0, reason: 'no usage samples', burn_per_task: null, tasks_left: null, eta_hours: null, confidence: 'none' }\n  33→  }\n  34→  const recent = samples.filter((r) => now - r.at <= 24 * 3600_000)\n  35→  const use = recent.length ? recent : samples.slice(-10)\n  36→  const burn = use.reduce((a, r) => a + r.cost, 0) / use.length\n  37→  const tokens = use.reduce((a, r) => a + r.input + r.output, 0) / use.length\n  38→  const spanHours = Math.max(1 / 60, (now - Math.min(...use.map((r) => r.at))) / 3600_000)\n  39→  const burnPerHour = use.reduce((a, r) => a + r.cost, 0) / spanHours\n  40→  let tasksLeft = null\n  41→  let etaHours = null\n  42→  if (quota && Number.isFinite(Number(quota.remaining_usd)) && burn > 0) {\n  43→    tasksLeft = Math.floor(Number(quota.remaining_usd) / burn)\n  44→    etaHours = burnPerHour > 0 ? Number(quota.remaining_usd) / burnPerHour : null\n  45→  } else if (quota && Number.isFinite(Number(quota.remaining)) && Number(quota.remaining) > 0 && tokens > 0 && quota.unit === 'tokens') {\n  46→    tasksLeft = Math.floor(Number(quota.remaining) / tokens)\n  47→  }\n  48→  const confidence = use.length >= 5 ? 'medium' : 'low'\n  49→  const risk = tasksLeft == null ? 'unknown' : tasksLeft <= 0 ? 'exhausted' : tasksLeft <= 2 ? 'critical' : tasksLeft <= 5 ? 'low_reserve' : 'ok'\n  50→  return {\n  51→    status: 'known', samples: use.length, burn_per_task: round(burn), tokens_per_task: Math.round(tokens),\n  52→    burn_per_hour: round(burnPerHour), tasks_left: tasksLeft, eta_hours: etaHours == null ? null : round(etaHours),\n  53→    confidence, risk,\n  54→  }\n  55→}\n  56→\n  57→function round(n) { return Math.round(n * 1e6) / 1e6 }\n  58→\n  59→const HOUR_MS = 3_600_000\n  60→\n  61→const USAGE_P = { Heavy: 0.9, Normal: 0.5, Light: 0.25 }\n  62→\n  63→export const DEFAULT_POLICY = {\n  64→  reading_ttl_s: 600,\n  65→  cache_read_weight: 0,\n  66→  usage_estimate_mtok: { Heavy: 2, Normal: 0.5, Light: 0.1 },\n  67→}\n  68→\n  69→function requireNow(now) {\n  70→  if (!Number.isFinite(now)) throw new TypeError('now must be a finite millisecond timestamp')\n  71→  return now\n  72→}\n  73→\n  74→function finiteNumber(value) {\n  75→  if (typeof value === 'number') return Number.isFinite(value) ? value : null\n  76→  return null\n  77→}\n  78→\n  79→function usageWeight(usage) {\n  80→  return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(USAGE_P, usage) ? USAGE_P[usage] : USAGE_P.Normal\n  81→}\n  82→\n  83→/** Nearest-rank quantile of the finite samples for a usage class; fewer than three samples is null. */\n  84→export function quantileForUsage(samples, usage) {\n  85→  const values = (Array.isArray(samples) ? samples : []).filter((item) => Number.isFinite(item))\n  86→  const n = values.length\n  87→  if (n < 3) return null\n  88→  const sorted = values.slice().sort((a, b) => a - b)\n  89→  const rank = Math.ceil(usageWeight(usage) * n) - 1\n  90→  return sorted[rank]\n  91→}\n  92→\n  93→/** Confidence from sample count, downgraded when the coefficient of variation exceeds one. */\n  94→export function confidenceFor(n, cv) {\n  95→  const count = Number.isFinite(n) ? n : 0\n  96→  if (count <= 0) return 'none'\n  97→  if (count < 5) return 'low'\n  98→  if (count < 20) return 'medium'\n  99→  return Number.isFinite(cv) && cv > 1 ? 'medium' : 'high'\n 100→}\n 101→\n 102→/** Risk from tasks left (tasks or usd basis) first, then the remaining fraction. */\n 103→export function classifyRisk({ tasks_left = null, tasks_left_basis = 'none', remaining_fraction = null } = {}) {\n 104→  if (Number.isFinite(tasks_left) && (tasks_left_basis === 'tasks' || tasks_left_basis === 'usd')) {\n 105→    const risk = tasks_left <= 0 ? 'exhausted' : tasks_left <= 2 ? 'critical' : tasks_left <= 5 ? 'low_reserve' : 'ok'\n 106→    return { risk, risk_basis: tasks_left_basis }\n 107→  }\n 108→  if (Number.isFinite(remaining_fraction)) {\n 109→    const risk = remaining_fraction <= 0 ? 'exhausted' : remaining_fraction < 0.05 ? 'critical' : remaining_fraction < 0.15 ? 'low_reserve' : 'ok'\n 110→    return { risk, risk_basis: 'fraction' }\n 111→  }\n 112→  return { risk: 'unknown', risk_basis: 'none' }\n 113→}\n 114→\n 115→/** Burn rate in Mtok per hour, clamped to at least one minute of elapsed time. */\n 116→export function burnMtokPerHour({ used_mtok = 0, hours_since_window_start = 0 } = {}) {\n 117→  const used = Number.isFinite(used_mtok) ? used_mtok : 0\n 118→  const hours = Number.isFinite(hours_since_window_start) ? hours_since_window_start : 0\n 119→  return round3(used / Math.max(hours, 1 / 60))\n 120→}\n 121→\n 122→/** Exhaustion instant and whether it lands strictly before the reset. */\n 123→export function etaExhaust({ now, remaining_mtok = 0, burn_mtok_per_hour = 0, reset_at = null } = {}) {\n 124→  const nowMs = requireNow(now)\n 125→  const remaining = Number.isFinite(remaining_mtok) ? remaining_mtok : 0\n 126→  const burn = Number.isFinite(burn_mtok_per_hour) ? burn_mtok_per_hour : 0\n 127→  const resetMs = typeof reset_at === 'string' ? Date.parse(reset_at) : Number.NaN\n 128→  const hasReset = Number.isFinite(resetMs)\n 129→\n 130→  let etaMs = null\n 131→  if (remaining <= 0) etaMs = nowMs\n 132→  else if (burn > 0) etaMs = nowMs + Math.round((remaining / burn) * HOUR_MS)\n 133→\n 134→  let exhausts = null\n 135→  if (hasReset) exhausts = etaMs === null ? false : etaMs < resetMs\n 136→\n 137→  return { eta_exhaust_at: etaMs === null ? null : new Date(etaMs).toISOString(), exhausts_before_reset: exhausts }\n 138→}\n 139→\n 140→function coefficientOfVariation(values) {\n 141→  if (!Array.isArray(values) || values.length < 2) return null\n 142→  const mean = values.reduce((total, value) => total + value, 0) / values.length\n 143→  if (mean === 0) return null\n 144→  const variance = values.reduce((total, value) => total + (value - mean) ** 2, 0) / values.length\n 145→  return Math.sqrt(variance) / mean\n 146→}\n 147→\n 148→function mergePolicy(policy) {\n 149→  const overrides = policy && typeof policy === 'object' ? policy : {}\n 150→  const merged = { ...DEFAULT_POLICY, ...overrides }\n 151→  const estimates = merged.usage_estimate_mtok && typeof merged.usage_estimate_mtok === 'object'\n 152→    ? merged.usage_estimate_mtok\n 153→    : DEFAULT_POLICY.usage_estimate_mtok\n 154→  merged.usage_estimate_mtok = estimates\n 155→  return merged\n 156→}\n 157→\n 158→function effectiveWindowStart(poolList, detail, nowMs) {\n 159→  const pool = poolList.find((item) => item && String(item.id ?? '') === detail.pool_id) ?? null\n 160→  const window = pool && pool.window && typeof pool.window === 'object' ? pool.window : null\n 161→  if (detail.reset_source === 'cli' && typeof detail.reset_at === 'string') {\n 162→    const resetMs = Date.parse(detail.reset_at)\n 163→    if (Number.isFinite(resetMs) && nowMs >= resetMs) return resetMs\n 164→  }\n 165→  if (window && typeof window.start_at === 'string') {\n 166→    const startMs = Date.parse(window.start_at)\n 167→    if (Number.isFinite(startMs)) return startMs\n 168→  }\n 169→  return null\n 170→}\n 171→\n 172→/**\n 173→ * The cliworker.forecast/v1 projection: remaining capacity, task estimate, risk, confidence,\n 174→ * burn and exhaustion time. All time arrives through `now`; nothing is read from the clock.\n 175→ */\n 176→export function buildForecast({\n 177→  model = '',\n 178→  quota = null,\n 179→  pools = null,\n 180→  rows = [],\n 181→  samples = [],\n 182→  usage = 'Normal',\n 183→  now,\n 184→  policy = null,\n 185→} = {}) {\n 186→  const nowMs = requireNow(now)\n 187→  const settings = mergePolicy(policy)\n 188→  const poolList = Array.isArray(pools) ? pools : []\n 189→  const sampleList = Array.isArray(samples) ? samples : []\n 190→\n 191→  let remaining_mtok = null\n 192→  let remaining_fraction = null\n 193→  let remaining_usd = null\n 194→  let fractionForRisk = null\n 195→  let quotaReason = null\n 196→  let evaluated = null\n 197→\n 198→  if (poolList.length > 0) {\n 199→    evaluated = evaluatePools({\n 200→      models: [model],\n 201→      pools: poolList,\n 202→      rows,\n 203→      now: nowMs,\n 204→      reading_ttl_s: settings.reading_ttl_s,\n 205→      cache_read_weight: settings.cache_read_weight,\n 206→    })\n 207→    const entry = evaluated[model]\n 208→    if (entry) {\n 209→      remaining_mtok = entry.remaining_mtok\n 210→      remaining_fraction = entry.remaining_fraction\n 211→      quotaReason = entry.reason\n 212→      const fractions = entry.pools\n 213→        .filter((item) => Number.isFinite(item.used_fraction))\n 214→        .map((item) => 1 - item.used_fraction)\n 215→      if (fractions.length > 0) fractionForRisk = Math.min(...fractions)\n 216→    }\n 217→    if (quota && Number.isFinite(quota.remaining_usd)) remaining_usd = quota.remaining_usd\n 218→  } else {\n 219→    const normalized = normalizeQuota(quota)\n 220→    remaining_mtok = normalized.remaining_mtok\n 221→    remaining_fraction = normalized.remaining_fraction\n 222→    remaining_usd = normalized.remaining_usd\n 223→    quotaReason = normalized.reason\n 224→  }\n 225→  if (fractionForRisk === null) fractionForRisk = remaining_fraction\n 226→\n 227→  const tokenSeries = []\n 228→  const costSeries = []\n 229→  for (const sample of sampleList) {\n 230→    if (!sample || typeof sample !== 'object') continue\n 231→    if (Number.isFinite(sample.mtok)) tokenSeries.push(sample.mtok)\n 232→    if (Number.isFinite(sample.cost_usd)) costSeries.push(sample.cost_usd)\n 233→  }\n 234→\n 235→  const tokens_per_task = {\n 236→    p25: quantileForUsage(tokenSeries, 'Light'),\n 237→    p50: quantileForUsage(tokenSeries, 'Normal'),\n 238→    p90: quantileForUsage(tokenSeries, 'Heavy'),\n 239→    n: tokenSeries.length,\n 240→  }\n 241→\n 242→  const tokenQuantile = quantileForUsage(tokenSeries, usage)\n 243→  const costQuantile = quantileForUsage(costSeries, usage)\n 244→\n 245→  let tasks_left = null\n 246→  let tasks_left_basis = 'none'\n 247→  if (remaining_mtok !== null && tokenQuantile !== null && tokenQuantile > 0) {\n 248→    tasks_left = Math.floor(remaining_mtok / tokenQuantile)\n 249→    tasks_left_basis = 'tasks'\n 250→  } else if (remaining_usd !== null && costQuantile !== null && costQuantile > 0) {\n 251→    tasks_left = Math.floor(remaining_usd / costQuantile)\n 252→    tasks_left_basis = 'usd'\n 253→  }\n 254→\n 255→  const estimate = finiteNumber(settings.usage_estimate_mtok[usage])\n 256→    ?? finiteNumber(settings.usage_estimate_mtok.Normal)\n 257→    ?? DEFAULT_POLICY.usage_estimate_mtok.Normal\n 258→  let tasks_left_assumed = null\n 259→  if (tasks_left === null && remaining_mtok !== null && estimate > 0) {\n 260→    tasks_left_assumed = Math.floor(remaining_mtok / estimate)\n 261→  }\n 262→\n 263→  let { risk, risk_basis } = classifyRisk({ tasks_left, tasks_left_basis, remaining_fraction: fractionForRisk })\n 264→  if (risk === 'unknown' && (remaining_mtok === 0 || remaining_usd === 0)) {\n 265→    risk = 'exhausted'\n 266→    risk_basis = 'none'\n 267→  }\n 268→\n 269→  if (tasks_left !== null && tasks_left < 0) tasks_left = 0\n 270→  if (tasks_left_assumed !== null && tasks_left_assumed < 0) tasks_left_assumed = 0\n 271→\n 272→  let cv = null\n 273→  if (tasks_left !== null) cv = coefficientOfVariation(tasks_left_basis === 'usd' ? costSeries : tokenSeries)\n 274→  const confidence = confidenceFor(sampleList.length, cv)\n 275→\n 276→  const known = remaining_mtok !== null || remaining_fraction !== null || remaining_usd !== null\n 277→  const status = known ? 'known' : 'unknown'\n 278→  if (!known) {\n 279→    risk = 'unknown'\n 280→    risk_basis = 'none'\n 281→  }\n 282→\n 283→  let reason = null\n 284→  if (!known) {\n 285→    reason = quotaReason ?? 'capacity_unknown'\n 286→  } else if (tasks_left === null) {\n 287→    const onlyUsd = remaining_mtok === null && remaining_fraction === null && remaining_usd !== null\n 288→    reason = onlyUsd ? 'usd_samples_missing' : 'no_samples'\n 289→  }\n 290→\n 291→  let burn_mtok_per_hour = null\n 292→  let eta_exhaust_at = null\n 293→  let exhausts_before_reset = null\n 294→  let poolDetails = []\n 295→\n 296→  if (evaluated && evaluated[model]) {\n 297→    poolDetails = evaluated[model].pools\n 298→    if (status === 'known') {\n 299→      let pick = null\n 300→      for (const item of poolDetails) {\n 301→        if (item.remaining_mtok === null) continue\n 302→        if (pick === null || item.remaining_mtok < pick.remaining_mtok) pick = item\n 303→      }\n 304→      if (pick) {\n 305→        const startMs = effectiveWindowStart(poolList, pick, nowMs)\n 306→        if (startMs !== null) {\n 307→          burn_mtok_per_hour = burnMtokPerHour({\n 308→            used_mtok: pick.used_mtok,\n 309→            hours_since_window_start: (nowMs - startMs) / HOUR_MS,\n 310→          })\n 311→          const eta = etaExhaust({\n 312→            now: nowMs,\n 313→            remaining_mtok: pick.remaining_mtok,\n 314→            burn_mtok_per_hour,\n 315→            reset_at: pick.reset_at,\n 316→          })\n 317→          eta_exhaust_at = eta.eta_exhaust_at\n 318→          exhausts_before_reset = eta.exhausts_before_reset\n 319→        }\n 320→      }\n 321→    }\n 322→  }\n 323→\n 324→  const burn_per_task = costSeries.length > 0\n 325→    ? round3(costSeries.reduce((total, value) => total + value, 0) / costSeries.length)\n 326→    : null\n 327→\n 328→  return {\n 329→    schema: 'cliworker.forecast/v1',\n 330→    status,\n 331→    model,\n 332→    remaining_mtok: remaining_mtok === null ? null : round3(remaining_mtok),\n 333→    remaining_fraction: remaining_fraction === null ? null : round3(remaining_fraction),\n 334→    pools: poolDetails.map((item) => ({\n 335→      pool_id: item.pool_id,\n 336→      remaining_mtok: item.remaining_mtok,\n 337→      remaining_fraction: item.remaining_fraction,\n 338→      reset_at: item.reset_at,\n 339→      reset_in_h: item.reset_in_h,\n 340→      reset_source: item.reset_source,\n 341→    })),\n 342→    tokens_per_task,\n 343→    tasks_left,\n 344→    tasks_left_basis,\n 345→    tasks_left_assumed,\n 346→    burn_mtok_per_hour,\n 347→    eta_exhaust_at,\n 348→    exhausts_before_reset,\n 349→    risk,\n 350→    risk_basis,\n 351→    confidence,\n 352→    reason,\n 353→    burn_per_task,\n 354→    samples: sampleList.length,\n 355→  }\n 356→}\n 357→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b76fcabd7d4ca301cf1d513a6538","_messageId":"01a1b771492a748abb3da2bc3fca2e36","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b76fcabd7d4ca301cf1d513a6538","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b771492a748abb3da2bc3fca2e36","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b771492a748abb3da2bc3fca2e36","traceparent":"00-c44ab554f795b9b062607ca3688ee7fa-85ce4a6cebf7295d-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b76f-c764-7902-805e-3362c00095cd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b76fcabd7d4ca301cf1d513a6538"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T19:17:00.543Z"}
{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b771-560a-7a59-8afe-f57bc3c0299a","session_id":"01a1b76f-c764-7902-805e-3362c00095cd","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2bf3bf9ad7fd32d","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→{\n   2→  \"task\": \"T-006\",\n   3→  \"milestone\": \"M1\",\n   4→  \"entries\": [\n   5→    {\n   6→      \"ac\": \"AC-015\",\n   7→      \"status\": \"covered\",\n   8→      \"files\": [\"test/unit/pools.test.mjs\", \"test/characterization/defects/a1-quota.test.mjs\"]\n   9→    },\n  10→    { \"ac\": \"AC-016\", \"status\": \"covered\", \"files\": [\"test/unit/pools.test.mjs\"] },\n  11→    { \"ac\": \"AC-017\", \"status\": \"covered\", \"files\": [\"test/unit/forecast-engine.test.mjs\"] },\n  12→    { \"ac\": \"AC-018\", \"status\": \"covered\", \"files\": [\"test/unit/forecast-unknown.test.mjs\"] },\n  13→    { \"ac\": \"AC-019\", \"status\": \"covered\", \"files\": [\"test/unit/reset.test.mjs\"] }\n  14→  ]\n  15→}\n  16→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b76fcabd7d4ca301cf1d513a6538","_messageId":"01a1b771492a748abb3da2bc3fca2e36","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b76fcabd7d4ca301cf1d513a6538","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b771492a748abb3da2bc3fca2e36","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b771492a748abb3da2bc3fca2e36","traceparent":"00-c44ab554f795b9b062607ca3688ee7fa-85ce4a6cebf7295d-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b76f-c764-7902-805e-3362c00095cd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b76fcabd7d4ca301cf1d513a6538"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T19:17:00.555Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b771-55d0-7b54-bed2-f20d227ed885","session_id":"01a1b76f-c764-7902-805e-3362c00095cd","message":{"id":"01a1b77155d07b54bed2f20b0947b5f3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me carefully verify the implementation against the design/spec. I need to be independent and thorough. Let me go through the design spec section by section and compare against the code.\n\nFirst, let me note a few things I want to verify carefully:\n\n1. **`normalizeQuota`** (design §3.4): \n   - `remaining_pct = p` → `remaining_fraction = clamp(p/100, 0, 1)`; `remaining_mtok` null. ✓ code does clamp01(percent/100).\n   - `remaining = r, unit='credits'`: `credits_per_mtok > 0` → `remaining_mtok = r/rate`; `r===0` → `remaining_mtok = 0`; else → null, reason `credits_conversion_missing`. Code: if rate>0 → r/rate; else if r===0 → 0; else reason. ✓. But note: what if r===0 AND rate>0? Design says `credits_per_mtok > 0 → remaining_mtok = r/rate` first. Code checks rate>0 first, so r/rate = 0. OK same result. Fine.\n   - Wait, there's a subtle issue: design says for credits with conversion missing, `reason: 'credits_conversion_missing'` but `remaining_mtok: null`. The code sets reason but leaves remaining_mtok null. Then `anyValue` check: remaining_fraction null, remaining_mtok null, remaining_usd null → but reason !== null so no capacity_unknown. Good. But what if there's ALSO a remaining_pct? Then anyValue is true (fraction set), and reason is still 'credits_conversion_missing'. Hmm. Design says fields computed independently; reason is set when credits conversion missing. Actually design says \"reason is only set when nothing usable could be read\" in the code comment (impl's comment), but the design §3.4 says reason: 'credits_conversion_missing' for the credits case. Let me think about whether this matters for golden. Probably fine.\n\n   Actually, let me check: normalizeQuota returns reason = 'credits_conversion_missing' even when remaining_pct also present (so remaining_fraction is non-null). Then in buildForecast (else branch), quotaReason = normalized.reason = 'credits_conversion_missing'. But status would be known (because fraction non-null). Then reason logic: `if (!known) reason = quotaReason` — but known is true, so reason stays null (or no_samples). The design §3.7 step 8: reason for known is no_samples or usd_samples_missing or null; quotasReason only used for unknown. So the credits_conversion_missing reason from normalizeQuota would be ignored when status known. That's consistent. Fine.\n\n2. **`round3`** (design §3.1): `sign * Math.round(Number((Math.abs(x) * 1000).toPrecision(15))) / 1000`, `+ 0` to kill -0. Non-finite passthrough. \n   - Code: `const number = Number(value); if (!Number.isFinite(number)) return value;` — Note it returns `value` (original), not `number`. Design says \"非有限数原样返回\" (return as-is). OK that matches \"原样返回\" — returns original value. Hmm, but if value is a string like \"abc\", Number(\"abc\")=NaN, returns \"abc\"? That's weird but golden probably only passes numbers. Let's check golden round3 cases. Actually, `Number(value)` for non-finite numbers returns the number. Fine.\n   - `Number((Math.abs(number) * 1000).toPrecision(15))`, `Math.round(magnitude)/1000`, `signed = number<0 ? -rounded : rounded`, `return signed + 0`. \n   - For x=0: magnitude = 0, rounded=0, signed=0 (0<0 false), 0+0 = 0 → positive zero. ✓\n   - For -0.0004: Math.abs=0.0004, *1000=0.4, toPrecision(15)=\"0.400000000000000\", Number=0.4, Math.round=0, /1000=0, signed = -0 (since number<0 → -0), -0 + 0 = 0 → positive zero. ✓ (design: round3(-0.0004) → 0). \n   - Hmm wait, but `-0` + `0`: in JS, `-0 + 0 = 0`. Yes positive zero. ✓\n   - 0.0625: *1000=62.5, toPrecision(15)=\"62.5000000000000\", Number=62.5, Math.round=63, /1000=0.063. ✓\n   - -0.0625: signed = -0.063. ✓\n\n3. **`billedTokens`** (design §3.1): row has finite `tokens` → use directly; else `input + output + cache_write + w*cache_read` (default 0), `w` default DEFAULT_POLICY.cache_read_weight (0). \n   - Code: `if (typeof row.tokens === 'number' && Number.isFinite(row.tokens)) return row.tokens`. Note: design says \"有限数字 tokens\" (finite number). Code checks typeof number. OK.\n   - `w` default param = DEFAULT_CACHE_READ_WEIGHT = 0. ✓ matches DEFAULT_POLICY.cache_read_weight 0.\n   - Returns input+output+written + w*read. ✓\n\n4. **`quantileForUsage`** (design §3.2): only finite numbers; n<3 → null; else sorted ascending, `sorted[ceil(p*n)-1]`; p: Heavy 0.9, Normal 0.5, Light 0.25; unknown usage → Normal; don't sort input in place. \n   - Code: filters `Number.isFinite(item)` — note this passes only numbers (strings would fail Number.isFinite). Design says \"只取有限数字\" (only finite numbers) — golden passes numbers. OK. Actually wait, design §3.2 says \"只取有限数字\" (only take finite numbers). But in buildForecast, tokenSeries is built with `Number.isFinite(sample.mtok)`. OK.\n   - `rank = Math.ceil(usageWeight(usage) * n) - 1`. ✓ usageWeight returns USAGE_P[usage] or Normal. ✓\n   - `sorted = values.slice().sort(...)` — doesn't mutate. ✓\n   - Returns sorted[rank]. But wait, nearest-rank: for Heavy with p=0.9 and n=3, ceil(0.9*3)=ceil(2.7)=3, rank=2 → sorted[2] = max. ✓ For Normal p=0.5, n=3, ceil(1.5)=2, rank=1 → median. ✓ For Light p=0.25, n=3, ceil(0.75)=1, rank=0 → min. ✓\n\n   Hmm, one concern: `Number.isFinite(item)` — if samples contains strings (from golden), they'd be filtered out. But design says only finite numbers. Let me check the golden files to be sure. Actually buildForecast passes tokenSeries (already numbers), but quantileForUsage is also called directly in A-10 via `quantileForUsage(input.samples, input.usage)`. So golden quantiles.json samples must be numbers. Let me verify.\n\n5. **`confidenceFor`** (design §3.2): n=0→none; 1..4→low; 5..19→medium; >=20→high, but cv finite >1 → high downgrades to medium (cv===1 no downgrade). cv only affects high. \n   - Code: `count <=0 → none`; `count<5 → low` (covers 1..4); `count<20 → medium` (5..19); else `cv>1 ? medium : high`. ✓. cv only used in the high branch. ✓ (n3-cv5 → count 3 → low, cv ignored). ✓\n\n6. **`burnMtokPerHour`** (design §3.2): `round3(used_mtok / max(hours, 1/60))`. \n   - Code: `round3(used / Math.max(hours, 1/60))`. ✓\n\n7. **`etaExhaust`** (design §3.2): \n   - `remaining_mtok <= 0` → `eta = now`; `burn <= 0` or non-finite → `eta_exhaust_at: null`; else `eta = now + round(remaining/burn*3600000)`. \n   - `exhausts_before_reset = eta < reset_ms` (strict); `reset_at` null → null; `eta_exhaust_at` null and remaining>0 → false.\n   - Code: `remaining <= 0 → etaMs = nowMs`; `else if (burn > 0) etaMs = nowMs + Math.round((remaining/burn)*HOUR_MS)`. Note: burn<=0 or non-finite → etaMs stays null. But what about remaining>0 and burn non-finite? `burn = Number.isFinite(burn_mtok_per_hour) ? ... : 0`, so non-finite → 0 → not >0 → etaMs null. ✓\n   - `exhausts`: `if (hasReset) exhausts = etaMs === null ? false : etaMs < resetMs`. So if reset_ms is null (no reset) → exhausts stays null. ✓. If etaMs null and hasReset → false. ✓ (design: eta_exhaust_at null and remaining>0 → false). Hmm but what if remaining<=0 (eta=now) and burn=0 and reset present → etaMs=nowMs, exhausts = now<resetMs. Fine.\n   - Wait, design says \"eta_exhaust_at 为 null 且剩余 > 0 → false\". But code: if hasReset and etaMs===null → false. That's regardless of remaining. But etaMs===null only happens when remaining>0 and burn<=0 (since remaining<=0 always gives etaMs=now). So effectively same. OK.\n   - `eta_exhaust_at = new Date(etaMs).toISOString()`. ✓. `new Date` with argument allowed.\n\n   Now A-10 checks: `etaExhaust({ now, remaining_mtok:5, burn:0, reset_at }) → { eta_exhaust_at: null, exhausts_before_reset: false }`. Code: remaining 5 >0, burn 0 not >0 → etaMs null; hasReset true → exhausts = false. Returns { eta_exhaust_at: null, exhausts_before_reset: false }. ✓\n\n8. **`classifyRisk`** (design §3.3): \n   - tasks/usd basis: <=0 exhausted, 1..2 critical, 3..5 low_reserve, >=6 ok. \n   - fraction: <=0 exhausted, <0.05 critical, <0.15 low_reserve, else ok (use unrounded value).\n   - priority tasks>usd>fraction>unknown: `tasks_left` finite and basis ∈ {tasks,usd} → tasks table, risk_basis = basis; else remaining_fraction finite → fraction table, risk_basis 'fraction'; else {unknown, none}. \n   - Code: `if (Number.isFinite(tasks_left) && (basis==='tasks'||basis==='usd'))` → risk based on tasks_left thresholds, risk_basis = tasks_left_basis. ✓. `if (Number.isFinite(remaining_fraction))` → fraction thresholds, risk_basis 'fraction'. ✓. else unknown/none. ✓\n   - \"tasks_left 为负数按 exhausted\" — code: `tasks_left <=0 ? exhausted`. ✓ (but note buildForecast clamps tasks_left to 0 before... actually classifyRisk is called BEFORE the clamp at line 269. Let me check order: line 263 `classifyRisk(...)` then line 269 clamp. So classifyRisk sees raw tasks_left which could be negative → exhausted. ✓. Actually floor of remaining/q where remaining could be... hmm remaining_mtok could be negative? Probably not in golden. Fine.)\n   - `classifyRisk` only returns {risk, risk_basis}. ✓\n\n   Wait — design says tasks table thresholds: `>=6 ok`, `3..5 low_reserve`, `1..2 critical`, `<=0 exhausted`. Code: `<=0 exhausted`, `<=2 critical`, `<=5 low_reserve`, else ok. For tasks_left=1 → 1<=0 no, 1<=2 yes → critical. ✓. For 3 → 3<=5 → low_reserve. ✓. For 6 → else ok. ✓. Note tasks_left is integer from floor, so ranges work. ✓\n\n   But hold on: design §3.3 says \"比较用未取整的值\" (comparison uses unrounded value) for fraction. buildForecast passes `fractionForRisk` which is computed from pools as `1 - used_fraction` (raw, unrounded) or from normalizeQuota `remaining_fraction` (clamp01(percent/100), raw). ✓. Let me double check fractionForRisk: in pools path, `fractions = entry.pools.filter(used_fraction finite).map(1 - used_fraction)`, `fractionForRisk = min(...fractions)`. used_fraction is state.used clamped (clamp01), not ro