reading: {value, at}`. Let me check. Actually A-7 uses `used_fraction: { value: 0.5, at: ... }` with no `reading` key → readingFor: pool.reading is undefined → skip first block; pool.used_fraction object → returns. ✓. So for golden, probably fine. But it's a spec deviation. However, the design's condition \"有对象 reading 且 value 为有限数\" — if reading exists but value not finite, then \"否则\" → check used_fraction. Code returns null. This could be a P2 finding if it affects any acceptance item. But does it affect any AC? Let me think about whether any golden case has a reading object with non-finite value AND a used_fraction. Probably not. It might be worth noting but let me focus on acceptance items. Actually, let me hold this thought; I'll verify against golden.\n\n  Actually, more importantly: A-7's `shaped` case has `used_fraction: { value: 0.5, ... }` and NO `reading` key. So readingFor returns the used_fraction. ✓. And `capacity_mtok: { 'claude:claude-sonnet-5-5': { value: 10 } }` → capacityFor returns 10. ✓. expected remaining 5. Let me trace: reading usable? reading.at = 09:55:00, now=10:00:00, ttl 600s=10min. now - reading.at = 5min = 300s <= 600s → usable. used = 0.5. rows = []. contributing none. remaining = 10*(1-0.5)=5. ✓.\n\n- Step 1 (有效重置): resolveResetAt. `reset_source==='cli'` and now>=reset_ms → effective window start = reset_ms, readings before reset_ms void, rows before reset_ms not counted. If not cli and now>=reset_ms → no change, pool detail `recheck: true`.\n  - Code `poolState`: `resetCandidates(pool)` derives cli/config/window. `resolveResetAt` → resolved {reset_at, reset_source}. `resetMs = timeMs(resolved.reset_at)`. `crossed = resetMs !== null && nowMs >= resetMs`. `cliReset = crossed && source==='cli'`. `recheck = crossed && source!=='cli'`. `windowStart = window.start_at`. `startMs = cliReset ? resetMs : windowStart`. \n  - `readingUsable`: reading !== null && !(cliReset && reading.at < resetMs) && nowMs - reading.at <= ttlMs. So for cliReset, readings before reset_ms are voided. ✓. For rows: in usable-reading branch, rows with `at > reading.at && at <= nowMs` counted. But design says \"早于 reset_ms 的行不计\" (rows before reset_ms not counted). Hmm. In the cliReset case, if reading is voided (because reading.at < resetMs), then we go to else branch (no usable reading), where `startMs = resetMs`, and rows with `at < startMs` are skipped. ✓. But if there IS a usable reading (reading.at >= resetMs) in cliReset case, then rows after reading.at are counted — those are all >= resetMs anyway. ✓. OK.\n  - Actually wait: in the usable-reading branch, the code doesn't explicitly filter `at < resetMs`. But since reading.at >= resetMs (for cliReset usable), rows counted are at > reading.at >= resetMs → fine. For non-cliReset, no reset filtering needed. ✓.\n\n  Let me check: design step 1 says \"若 reset_source === 'cli' 且 now >= reset_ms：该池的有效窗口起点改为 reset_ms，早于 reset_ms 的读数视为作废、早于 reset_ms 的行不计\". Code handles via startMs and readingUsable. ✓.\n\n- Step 2 reading fresh: reading exists, not voided, and `now - reading.at <= ttl`. \n  - Code readingUsable. ✓. Note design says \"reading 存在、未作废\" — but code uses `reading !== null` which means a reading object with finite value and valid at. ✓.\n\n- Step 3 used_p:\n  - fresh reading: `reading.value + Σ(at > reading.at && at <= now 的行的 tokens_i / (cap_p(model_i)*1e6))`. \n    - Code: `used = reading.value`; for rows with `at > reading.at && at <= nowMs` → contributing. Then summing billedTokens/(capacity*1e6). ✓.\n  - else: window (`start_at <= at <= now`, start from step 1 effective start) all rows summed. No window and rows needing count → `unknown(window_unknown)`.\n    - Code else branch: relevant = rows with `at <= nowMs` and (`startMs===null || at >= startMs`). If `startMs === null && relevant.length > 0` → reason = 'window_unknown'. else used=0 and contributing = relevant. \n    - Hmm, design says window is `start_at <= at <= now`. Code uses `at >= startMs` (includes s