is round3(min fractions)). Then output `round3(remaining_fraction)` again (double round3, harmless). ✓. And `fractionForRisk` uses raw 1-used_fraction from pools for risk. ✓.\n\nHmm wait — but design §3.7 step 1 says \"剩余量: pools 非空 → evaluatePools(...)[model]（remaining_mtok、remaining_fraction、reason）\". And step 5 risk uses `classifyRisk({..., remaining_fraction})`. Which remaining_fraction? The design §3.5 says `remaining_fraction = round3(min_p (1-used_p))`. But §3.3 note says \"classifyRisk 的 fraction 比较用未取整值\". Hmm. There's a tension: if buildForecast passes the rounded `remaining_fraction` (0.5) to classifyRisk, is that a problem? For the boundary 0.15 case (A-11), that's the quota path (no pools), where `remaining_fraction` from normalizeQuota is raw 0.15 (clamp01(15/100)=0.15 exactly). classificyRisk uses fractionForRisk = remaining_fraction = 0.15 (unrounded). ✓. For pools path with fraction near 0.05 or 0.15 boundary... the code uses fractionForRisk = min(1 - used_fraction) raw. So it uses unrounded. ✓. Good, that's why they compute fractionForRisk separately. Smart. ✓.\n\nOK now let me look at buildForecast more carefully.\n\nbuildForecast:\n- Step 1 remaining: pools path computes remaining_mtok, remaining_fraction, quotaReason from evaluatePools; `remaining_fraction = entry.remaining_fraction` (round3 value). `fractionForRisk` from pools raw. Then `if (quota && Number.isFinite(quota.remaining_usd)) remaining_usd = quota.remaining_usd`. ✓ (quota.remaining_usd as usd remaining). \n  - Note: design says \"两者都给时以 pools 为准，且 quota.remaining_usd 仍可作为 usd 剩余量\". ✓.\n- Step 2 samples: tokenSeries (mtok finite), costSeries (cost_usd finite). `tokens_per_task = {p25,p50,p90,n}` with Light/Normal/Heavy quantiles, n = tokenSeries.length. ✓.\n- Step 3 tasks_left: \n  - `remaining_mtok !== null && tokenQuantile !== null && tokenQuantile > 0` → floor(remaining_mtok/tokenQuantile), basis 'tasks'. ✓.\n  - else `remaining_usd !== null && costQuantile !== null && costQuantile > 0` → floor(remaining_usd/costQuantile), basis 'usd'. ✓.\n  - else null, 'none'. ✓.\n  - Note design: \"取用户 usage 对应分位数 q，q>0\". ✓.\n- Step 4 tasks_left_assumed: only when tasks_left===null && remaining_mtok !== null → floor(remaining_mtok / policy.usage_estimate_mtok[usage]). \n  - Code: `estimate = finiteNumber(settings.usage_estimate_mtok[usage]) ?? finiteNumber(Normal) ?? DEFAULT Normal`. Then `if (tasks_left===null && remaining_mtok!==null && estimate>0) tasks_left_assumed = floor(remaining_mtok/estimate)`. ✓. \n  - Design: \"否则 null。tasks_left 非 null 时它为 null\". ✓.\n- Step 5 risk: classifyRisk(...) then zero-remaining rule: if risk unknown and (remaining_mtok===0 || remaining_usd===0) → {exhausted, none}. ✓. \n  - \"写出的 tasks_left 与 tasks_left_assumed 只允许 null 或 ≥0 的整数（schema minimum）；Math.floor 结果为负时写 0\". Code clamps both to 0 if <0. ✓.\n  - Hmm wait: classifyRisk is called with `tasks_left` BEFORE clamping. If tasks_left is negative, classifyRisk returns exhausted. Then zero-remaining rule wouldn't change. Then clamp to 0. OK consistent with \"tasks_left 为负数按 exhausted\". ✓.\n- Step 6 confidence: confidenceFor(n, cv), n = samples.length (not filtered). cv from the series that produced tasks_left; null when tasks_left null, series length<2, or mean===0; else sqrt(sum((x-mean)^2)/n)/mean (population std, divide by n). \n  - Code: `cv = tasks_left !== null ? coefficientOfVariation(tasks_left_basis==='usd' ? costSeries : tokenSeries) : null`. `confidence = confidenceFor(sampleList.length, cv)`. ✓.\n  - `coefficientOfVariation`: `values.length<2 → null`; mean===0 → null; `variance = sum((x-mean)^2)/values.length`; `sqrt(variance)/mean`. ✓ (divide by n). ✓.\n  - Hmm, design says \"n = samples.length（不是过滤后的序列长度）\". Code uses sampleList.length. ✓. But cv uses the filtered series (costSeries/tokenSeries). Design: \"cv 取参与 tasks_left 的那条序列\". ✓. But note: the cv series length could be < sampleList.length (if some samples have null mtok). The variance divides by 