{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b775-296f-7afd-9b34-dac3a881b1ad","session_id":"01a1b76f-c764-7902-805e-3362c00095cd","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a503c513660b3762","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→import test from 'node:test'\n   2→import assert from 'node:assert/strict'\n   3→import fs from 'node:fs'\n   4→\n   5→import { normalizeQuota, remainingForModels } from '../../lib/pools.mjs'\n   6→import { buildForecast } from '../../lib/forecast.mjs'\n   7→\n   8→const shapes = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(new URL('../../contracts/golden/quota-shapes.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8'))\n   9→const pools = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(new URL('../../contracts/golden/b44.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8'))\n  10→\n  11→for (const item of shapes.cases) {\n  12→  test(`[AC-015] ${item.id}`, () => {\n  13→    const actual = buildForecast({\n  14→      quota: item.input.quota,\n  15→      samples: item.input.samples,\n  16→      usage: item.input.usage,\n  17→      now: 0,\n  18→    })\n  19→    for (const key of Object.keys(item.expected)) {\n  20→      assert.deepStrictEqual(actual[key], item.expected[key], `${item.id} ${key}`)\n  21→    }\n  22→  })\n  23→}\n  24→\n  25→test('[AC-015] golden case count', () => {\n  26→  assert.equal(shapes.cases.length, 9)\n  27→})\n  28→\n  29→test('[AC-015] normalizeQuota percentage shape', () => {\n  30→  assert.deepStrictEqual(normalizeQuota({ remaining_pct: 5 }), {\n  31→    remaining_fraction: 0.05,\n  32→    remaining_mtok: null,\n  33→    remaining_usd: null,\n  34→    reason: null,\n  35→  })\n  36→  assert.deepStrictEqual(normalizeQuota({ remaining_pct: 240 }), {\n  37→    remaining_fraction: 1,\n  38→    remaining_mtok: null,\n  39→    remaining_usd: null,\n  40→    reason: null,\n  41→  })\n  42→})\n  43→\n  44→test('[AC-015] normalizeQuota credits shape', () => {\n  45→  assert.deepStrictEqual(normalizeQuota({ remaining: 2, unit: 'credits', credits_per_mtok: 1000 }), {\n  46→    remaining_fraction: null,\n  47→    remaining_mtok: 0.002,\n  48→    remaining_usd: null,\n  49→    reason: null,\n  50→  })\n  51→  assert.deepStrictEqual(normalizeQuota({ remaining: 1, unit: 'credits' }), {\n  52→    remaining_fraction: null,\n  53→    remaining_mtok: null,\n  54→    remaining_usd: null,\n  55→    reason: 'credits_conversion_missing',\n  56→  })\n  57→  assert.deepStrictEqual(normalizeQuota({ remaining: 0, unit: 'credits' }), {\n  58→    remaining_fraction: null,\n  59→    remaining_mtok: 0,\n  60→    remaining_usd: null,\n  61→    reason: null,\n  62→  })\n  63→})\n  64→\n  65→test('[AC-015] normalizeQuota tokens shape', () => {\n  66→  assert.deepStrictEqual(normalizeQuota({ remaining: 2500000, unit: 'tokens' }), {\n  67→    remaining_fraction: null,\n  68→    remaining_mtok: 2.5,\n  69→    remaining_usd: null,\n  70→    reason: null,\n  71→  })\n  72→})\n  73→\n  74→test('[AC-015] normalizeQuota usd shape', () => {\n  75→  assert.deepStrictEqual(normalizeQuota({ remaining_usd: 3 }), {\n  76→    remaining_fraction: null,\n  77→    remaining_mtok: null,\n  78→    remaining_usd: 3,\n  79→    reason: null,\n  80→  })\n  81→})\n  82→\n  83→test('[AC-015] normalizeQuota missing shape', () => {\n  84→  assert.deepStrictEqual(normalizeQuota({}), {\n  85→    remaining_fraction: null,\n  86→    remaining_mtok: null,\n  87→    remaining_usd: null,\n  88→    reason: 'capacity_unknown',\n  89→  })\n  90→  assert.deepStrictEqual(normalizeQuota(null), {\n  91→    remaining_fraction: null,\n  92→    remaining_mtok: null,\n  93→    remaining_usd: null,\n  94→    reason: 'capacity_unknown',\n  95→  })\n  96→})\n  97→\n  98→for (const item of pools.cases) {\n  99→  test(`[AC-016] ${item.id}`, () => {\n 100→    const actual = remainingForModels({\n 101→      models: item.input.models,\n 102→      pools: item.input.pools,\n 103→      rows: item.input.rows,\n 104→      now: Date.parse(item.input.now),\n 105→      reading_ttl_s: item.input.reading_ttl_s,\n 106→    })\n 107→    assert.deepStrictEqual(actual, item.expected, item.id)\n 108→  })\n 109→}\n 110→\n 111→test('[AC-016] golden case count', () => {\n 112→  assert.equal(pools.cases.length, 9)\n 113→})\n 114→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b76fcabd7d4ca301cf1d513a6538","_messageId":"01a1b77518b171ab9b1f582b10dd1c6e","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b76fcabd7d4ca301cf1d513a6538","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b77518b171ab9b1f582b10dd1c6e","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b77518b171ab9b1f582b10dd1c6e","traceparent":"00-c44ab554f795b9b062607ca3688ee7fa-85ce4a6cebf7295d-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b76f-c764-7902-805e-3362c00095cd,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b76fcabd7d4ca301cf1d513a6538"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T19:21:11.279Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b775-293b-7644-8412-20b80d9aa4e0","session_id":"01a1b76f-c764-7902-805e-3362c00095cd","message":{"id":"01a1b775293b7644841220b6312342b9","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"These are genuine tests. The golden quota-shapes values match design (e.g., q-pct-5 → 0.05, low_reserve, fraction; q-credits-rate → remaining_mtok 0.001, tasks_left 0, exhausted, tasks basis; q-usd → tasks_left 6, usd basis). ✓ Consistent with brief AC-015 and design §3.4.\n\nWait — one thing: q-credits-rate expects `remaining_mtok: 0.001` and `tasks_left: 0` with `risk: exhausted`, `risk_basis: tasks`. Let me verify buildForecast: quota remaining=1, credits_per_mtok=1000 → remaining_mtok = 1/1000 = 0.001. samples 3× 0.2 mtok → tokenQuantile (Normal) = 0.2. tasks_left = floor(0.001/0.2) = 0. basis tasks. classifyRisk(tasks_left=0, basis tasks) → exhausted, basis tasks. ✓. output remaining_mtok round3(0.001)=0.001 ✓.\n\nq-credits-zero: remaining=0, credits → remaining_mtok=0. samples empty. tokenQuantile null → tasks_left null. risk: classifyRisk with remaining_fraction=null → unknown. zero-remaining rule: risk unknown && remaining_mtok===0 → exhausted, basis none. expected only risk exhausted. ✓.\n\nOK. Now let me check the other test files and golden forecast files. Let me read them. Actually, let me think about what else could be a problem.\n\nHmm, an important thing: I noticed `billedTokens` uses `typeof row.tokens === 'number'`. But design §3.5 says rows have `tokens | input_tokens…`. And A-7's `run(w)` case has row with `input_tokens` and `cache_read_tokens`, and `reading: null`. Let me check the b44 golden to make sure rows use the tokens field shape. Actually CI A-6 and A-7 passed, so fine.\n\nLet me now check the forecast golden files and the other test files. Let me batch read.","signature":""}],"model":"hy4-free","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_in