ays \"早于 reset_ms 的行不计\" for cli crossing. In the fresh-reading branch (when reading is usable), rows are filtered by `at > reading.at`. If cliReset and reading.at >= resetMs (usable), then all counted rows are > reading.at >= resetMs. ✓. But what if cliReset and reading is voided (reading.at < resetMs)? Then readingUsable false → else branch, startMs = resetMs, rows with at < startMs skipped. ✓.\n\nHmm, but what about `b44-stale-reading-uses-ledger`? Let me check that golden case. \"读数过期后改用账本时 reason 为 null\" (design §1.1 item 3: b44 golden requires reason null, no reading_stale). Let me verify: in poolState, if reading is stale (now - reading.at > ttl), readingUsable false → else branch. If window start exists → used computed from rows, reason null. ✓. So reason null. ✓. Good, no reading_stale produced.\n\nLet me read b44.json now.\n\nActually, let me step back. I've verified a LOT. The implementation looks solid and consistent with design. CI passed all 15 AC commands. All hashes match. Static gates (R-3, R-4) pass. test files are genuine. Golden files frozen and consistent.\n\nNow the remaining question: R-1, R-2, R-5 gates (which require running scripts) — no CI evidence. Let me think about how to handle. \n\nGiven the instruction \"只有 CI 结果缺失、或与代码明显矛盾时，才把该项标为无法确认并写 finding\" — I'm now fairly convinced this means: if a CI result is missing for an acceptance item, mark it \"无法确认\" and write a finding. But that would force needs_revision for R-1..R-5. Hmm, but that seems to contradict the spirit that \"your env limitations can't be a reason to fail\". Let me re-read once more very carefully:\n\n\"你的评审环境可能缺 pwsh 7、或缺临时文件权限——这不能作为判 needs_revision 的理由。只有 CI 结果缺失、或与代码明显矛盾时，才把该项标为无法确认并写 finding；其余请用只读方式（读文件、算哈希、核对行号）独立验证实现与规格是否一致。\"\n\nI think the correct parse is:\n- \"Your review env may lack pwsh7 or temp-file perms — this can't be a reason to judge needs_revision.\" → Don't fail because YOU can't run commands.\n- \"Only when CI results are missing, or clearly cont