s test/. Only pools.test.mjs and a1-quota.test.mjs should have it. Let me verify — important because if a third file had `[AC-015]`, filtered would be 3 files and A-1 would fail. CI A-1 passed, so it's 2. But let me confirm read-only. Also, the design says \"每个新建的测试文件只写自己负责的 [AC-xxx] 标签\" (each new test file only writes its own AC tag) and \"pools.test.mjs 同时写 AC-015 与 AC-016\". Let me grep to confirm no cross-contamination (e.g., forecast-engine.test.mjs shouldn't contain [AC-015]).\n\n2. **AC-017 A-9 expects `run-tests: filtered 1 files`** and 12 titles including `[AC-017] thresholds golden case count` etc. forecast-engine.test.mjs has those. ✓ (I saw the four case-count titles). Let me verify all 12 titles exist. CI A-9 passed. Fine.\n\n3. **Golden case counts** — verified: 9,9,21,15,11,14. ✓. And test titles `[AC-017] thresholds golden case count` etc. — the test file uses `test(\\`[AC-017] ${golden.label} golden case count\\`, ...)` with labels thresholds/quantiles/confidence/burn-eta. ✓ exact titles.\n\n4. **`--ac AC-016` selects only pools.test.mjs** — need forecast files to NOT contain `[AC-016]`. Let me grep.\n\nLet me do a grep for all `[AC-0xx]` tags per test file to confirm the tagging discipline. This is a good independent check.\n\n5. **A-2 buildForecast deep equality on 9 quota-shapes cases** — I verified the code logic produces expected values. CI passed. Let me spot-check a tricky one: q-pct-4 → remaining_fraction 0.04, risk critical, basis fraction. classifyRisk(0.04): 0.04 <= 0? no; 0.04 < 0.05 → critical. ✓. q-pct-15 → 0.15: 0.15 < 0.05 no, 0.15 < 0.15 no → ok. ✓. q-pct-0 → 0: <=0 → exhausted. ✓. q-credits-no-rate → risk unknown, basis none, reason credits_conversion_missing. buildForecast: normalizeQuota → remaining_mtok null, remaining_fraction null, remaining_usd null, reason credits_conversion_missing. status unknown → risk unknown, basis none. reason = quotaReason = credits_conversion_missing. ✓. Note: A-2 only checks keys in expected, so risk/risk_basis/reason. ✓.\n\nWait — q-credits-no-rate expects `risk: unknown, risk_basis: none, reason: credits_conversion_missing`. But the zero-remaining rule: `risk === 'unknown' && (remaining_mtok === 0 || remaining_usd === 0)` → exhausted. Here remaining_mtok is null (not 0), remaining_usd null → stays unknown. ✓.\n\n6. **q-usd**: remaining_usd 3, samples 3× cost 0.5, mtok null. tokenSeries empty → tokenQuantile null. costSeries = [0.5,0.5,0.5], costQuantile (Normal) = 0.5. tasks_left = floor(3/0.5) = 6, basis usd. classifyRisk(6, usd) → 6 > 5 → ok, basis usd. ✓. But wait — `remaining_mtok` is null, `remaining_fraction` null, `remaining_usd` 3 → status known. reason: tasks_left !== null → null. burn/eta: no pools → null. ✓. And `tasks_left_assumed`: tasks_left !== null → null. ✓. confidence: cv from costSeries (3 values all 0.5) → mean 0.5, variance 0 → cv 0; confidenceFor(sampleList.length=3, 0) → count 3 <5 → low. Golden doesn't check confidence. ✓.\n\n7. **A-8 buildForecast b44-reading-half** — I verified the hand calc gives exactly the expected (burn 1.667, eta 12:59:57.840Z, pools six fields). Let me double-check `reset_source: 'config'`: window has no reset_source → resetCandidates: `source = win.reset_source ?? null` = null → returns config = win.reset_at. resolveResetAt with config → reset_source 'config'. ✓. And `reset_in_h`: (12:00 - 10:00)/3600000 = 2 → round3(2)=2. ✓. `remaining_fraction` for the pool = round3(1-0.5) = 0.5. ✓.\n\nHmm, one thing: A-8 expects `remaining_fraction: 0.5` at top level. buildForecast sets `remaining_fraction = entry.remaining_fraction` = round3(min fractions) = 0.5, then output round3(0.5)=0.5. ✓. And `fractionForRisk` = 1 - 0.5 = 0.5 (raw) → classifyRisk → ok, basis fraction. ✓.\n\n8. **The pools output in buildForecast** maps six fields. ✓. A-8 checks `Object.keys(actual.pools[0]).sort()` equals the six. ✓.\n\n9. **R-3** — `lib/forecast.mjs` systemNow count exactly 2. Verified. And no Date.now. pools.mjs no banned words. ✓. But also check: \"零参数 new Date()\" — check-seams covers. The code uses `new Date(ms)` with args. Let me verify: pools.mjs `new Date(ms).toISOString()` (with arg) and `new Date(resetMs)`. forecast.mjs `new Date(etaMs).toISOString()`. All with args. ✓. And check-seams: ok (files=20) directly confirms no violations. ✓.\n\n10. **R-4** — no token-like strings in 8 files. Verified. ✓.\n\n11. **AC-018 A-13** — checks four outputs pass schema. I verified buildForecast returns all 19 required fields with valid types. Note: validate.mjs — need to check it handles `additionalProperties: true` and the schema's constraints correctly. CI A-13 passed. ✓.\n\nActually, let me double check one potential schema issue: `tokens_per_task` — buildForecast always returns `{p25,p50,p90,n}` object (never null). Schema allows object or null. ✓. `pools` — array of six-field objects. Schema requires those six fields. ✓. `tasks_left`/`tasks_left_assumed` clamped ≥0 integers. ✓. `risk` enum values. ✓. `reason` enum includes null + the reasons. ✓. `risk_basis` enum. ✓. `confidence` enum. ✓. `samples` integer ≥0. ✓. `model` string. ✓. `status` enum. ✓. `schema` const. ✓. All good.\n\nHmm, wait: `eta_exhaust_at` — schema type string|null. buildForecast returns null or ISO string. ✓. `exhausts_before_reset` boolean|null. ✓. `burn_mtok_per_hour` number|null. ✓. `burn_per_task` number|null. ✓. `remaining_mtok`/`remaining_fraction` number|null. ✓.\n\n12. **The `reason` enum in schema** includes `reading_stale` but design §1.1 item 3 says T-006 doesn't produce it. buildForecast never produces reading_stale. ✓.\n\nOK, now let me check the AC tag discipline grep. Let me also verify the b44.json content matches design (spot check a few expected values), and check the forecast golden files briefly (e.g., round3 cases, eta cases) to confirm design consistency. Actually, since golden hashes match the frozen manifest and CI A-6/A-10 passed, and the code implements the design formulas, I'm fairly confident. B