on is enough.\n\nLet me compute sha256 of ci-results.json and the git sha verification once more, and also gather exact line numbers for the code references I'll cite (file:line). I have line numbers from the Read outputs. Good.\n\nLet me also double-check: the user wants \"每条结论的证据（命令输出或文件行号）\" — evidence for each conclusion (command output or file line numbers). So each `checks` entry should have either a command output (CI lastLine / my run output) or file line numbers. I'll include both where possible. For the 15 AC items: cite ci-results.json line numbers (e.g., `ci-results.json:9-17`) + lastLine + exitCode, PLUS independent read-only verification with file line numbers (e.g., `lib/forecast.mjs:176-356`, `test/unit/pools.test.mjs:11-27`). For gates: cite my direct command outputs.\n\nLet me get the exact ci-results.json line ranges for each of the 15 results. From the Read output:\n- A-1: lines 9-17\n- A-2: 18-26\n- A-3: 27-35\n- A-4: 36-44\n- A-5: 45-53\n- A-6: 54-62\n- A-7: 63-71\n- A-8: 72-80\n- A-9: 81-89\n- A-10: 90-98\n- A-11: 99-107\n- A-12: 108-116\n- A-13: 117-125\n- A-14: 126-134\n- A-15: 135-143\n- Header passed/total/ok: lines 5-7.\n\nLet me now also compute the sha256 of ci-results.json for evidence.\n\nAlso, I realize I should double check the CI A-1..A-15 \"output\" fields — they're all just the OK line. Let me verify there's no `✖` (10006) in outputs — the commands check that; CI passed so fine. Also \"fail 0\" — the filtered runs produce `fail 0`; the ci-results output field is only \"AC-015 OK\" because the command captures that internally. Hmm — wait, actually A-1's command doesn't print the run-tests output at all (it captures `o` internally and only checks conditions). So the CI \"output\" field = \"AC-015 OK\" only. That's what ci-results shows. Fine. The user says these are valid evidence; I'll cite exitCode=0 + lastLine.\n\nLet me now also double-check: did I verify that ci-results.json doesn't have all-false or something? All passed=true